# TypeScript/TSX Style Preferences

- Prefer minimal type declarations; do not add extra local types/interfaces when inference is clear.
- Especially around DB/tRPC results, avoid redundant mirror types unless they add real safety or readability.

- Keep vertical spacing readable:
  - Leave blank lines between logical code blocks (imports, state/hooks, handlers, JSX sections).
  - Do not over-condense code into dense blocks.

- Prefer arrow functions for most declarations (helpers, handlers, callbacks, exported non-page components).
- Use normal function declarations for page-level components in `src/app/**/page.tsx`.

- When editing existing files, follow the local spacing and formatting pattern already present in that file.
